      ],
      "kind": "book",
      "label": "A swollen diary",
      "model": "book",
      "codex": "berez_burgomaster_diary",
      "flag": "berez_diary_read",
      "text": "The last pages of the diary of Ivo Dragan, burgomaster of Berez, the ink run with damp. He writes that the lord of the castle has been calling on Marina, the candlemaker's girl, with gifts nobody dares refuse. He hid her in the chapel, under the bell, and sat up with her. In the morning she was dead in her blankets, not a mark on her, only a scratch over the heart like a bramble's. The last entry is one line: The river is coming up the street, and the bell is ringing on its own."
    },
